 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "request and health are equal-length lists of positive integers and k is a positive integer. Time runs in rounds. In each round every server that is still up handles request[i] requests, all of which count towards the total; then one chosen server that is still up loses k health and goes down when its health reaches 0 or less. Return the minimum possible total number of requests handled before every server is down.",
